From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 047/185] segacd: restart the CDD when it stops reporting

Established by elimination rather than guessed at. The watchdog fired,
so the interrupt stopped -- but the storm guard did not mask it (that
prints 'S', which is tested first and has a glyph), no other write to
the mask is destructive (every one is an OR, and levels 2 and 3 are
demonstrably still being taken), and HOCK is never cleared (the only
value ever written to the control register is 4, which sets it).

So the drive stopped reporting. That also explains the one thing that
never fitted: the standalone test runs seconds after the disc was last
read, with it still spinning, while EmuTOS reaches its desktop a long
idle later.

HOCK is documented as "starts communication with the CDD", so the
watchdog now sets it again while stalled, and stops the moment packets
return. The command counter shows wake attempts instead of sends while
stalled, since a stalled link sends nothing worth counting.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 66b9213..a2c9173 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -130,6 +130,7 @@ static UBYTE cdd_stat[10];
 static ULONG cdd_rawbuf[3];     /* aligned: the read below is long-wide */
 #define cdd_raw ((UBYTE *)cdd_rawbuf)
 static UBYTE cdd_valid;         /* last packet checksummed */
+static UBYTE cdd_wakes;         /* attempts to restart a stopped drive */
 static UBYTE cdd_stalled;       /* the score is zero because the interrupt
                                  * stopped, not because packets are bad --
                                  * one character cannot mean both */
@@ -698,6 +699,28 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
     } else if (cdd_quiet < 255 && ++cdd_quiet >= 8) {
         cdd_score = 0;          /* eight VBLs is six missed packets */
         cdd_stalled = 1;
+
+        /* ...and try to start it again.
+         *
+         * Nothing on our side masked the interrupt: the storm guard did
+         * not fire, every other write to the mask is an OR, and levels
+         * 2 and 3 are demonstrably still being taken, so the mask is
+         * intact. We never clear HOCK either -- the only value written
+         * to the control register is 4, which sets it. By elimination
+         * the drive itself stopped reporting, which fits the one thing
+         * that never made sense: the standalone test runs seconds after
+         * the disc was last read, and EmuTOS runs a minute later with
+         * the drive left idle.
+         *
+         * HOCK is documented as "starts communication with the CDD", so
+         * setting it again is the documented way to ask for it back.
+         * Once every eight frames while stalled, and it stops the
+         * moment packets return. */
+        if (cdd_quiet >= 8) {
+            cdd_quiet = 8;      /* stay stalled; keep prodding */
+            *CDD_CTRL_B = CDD_HOCK;
+            cdd_wakes++;
+        }
     }
 
     /* Two counters that must both be spinning, because between them
@@ -747,7 +770,7 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
         | (cdd_cmd_on ? 0x80 : 0)
         | ((UWORD)(cdd_stormed ? 1 : 0) << 8)
         | ((UWORD)((cdd_ctrl | (cdd_ctrl_ever << 2)) & 0x07) << 9)
-        | ((UWORD)(cdd_sent & 0x07) << 12)
+        | ((UWORD)((cdd_stalled ? cdd_wakes : cdd_sent) & 0x07) << 12)
         | (cdd_stalled ? 0x8000 : 0));
 
     if (pcm_countdown) {                /* silence the bell when it is due */
